@page "/settings"
@layout AppLayout
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Pages.Student
@attribute [Authorize]

@*
    SettingsPage — owns the /settings route and nothing else.

    The route is shared by two entirely separate experiences:

      Student            -> StudentProfilePage, the finalized Motiva
                            "הפרופיל שלי" screen.
      Mentor / Lecturer
      / Admin            -> StaffProfilePage, the same screen built on the
                            role-neutral /api/users/me payload.

    Splitting here rather than branching inside one component keeps the two
    apart at every level — markup, scoped CSS, lifecycle and API calls — so
    neither panel loads the other's data. That mattered most when the second
    branch was the legacy screen; it still holds now that both are Motiva,
    because /api/student/me is Student-gated and /api/users/me is not.

    THE STAFF BRANCH CHANGED, THE SPLIT DID NOT. It used to render
    StaffSettingsPage — the pre-Motiva `spp-*` screen on the `--g-*` tokens,
    which inside `.motiva-final` resolves the right colours at the wrong
    geometry and so read as a different product from every other page in the
    same shell. StaffProfilePage is that screen rebuilt on the student
    profile's approved structure. StaffSettingsPage.razor is left on disk,
    unreferenced, so the migration can still be read against it; nothing
    routes to it any more.

    The URL is deliberately unchanged. Students already reach it from the
    profile control in the top nav, Mentor / Lecturer / Admin from their "הגדרות" nav item,
    and every one of those entry points keeps working untouched.
*@

@if (_user is null)
{
    @* _user cascades in asynchronously from App.razor and is null on the
       first render. Rendering nothing here — rather than defaulting to one
       of the two panels — is what stops a student briefly mounting the staff
       page and firing its /api/users/me + mentor-preferences calls before
       auth state resolves. *@
}
else if (RoleService.IsStudent(_user))
{
    <StudentProfilePage />
}
else
{
    <StaffProfilePage />
}

@code {
    [CascadingParameter] private User? _user { get; set; }
}
